n and Fonoimoana faced another set of Portuguese-speakers, but were not expected to defeat the second Brazilian team of " [:a {:href "/athletes/51905"} "Zé Marco"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/94350"} "Ricardo"] ". They had played four times previously and the Brazilians had won every match. In the final, Zé Marco and Ricardo got off to an early lead in the first set, but the Americans came from behind to win 12-11. They led throughout the second set and won the gold medal in straight sets, 12-11 and 12-9. The German bronze medal by Jörg Ahmann and Axel Hager was a surprise as they were seeded only 15th and had qualified for the Olympics only the month before the Games."] "\n"] [:button {:id "button712053", :class "btn btn-default"} "Details"] [:script {} "$('#button712053').click(splits)"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Matches Played"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Wins"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Losses"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Sets"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Points"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Faults"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Service Aces"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Fastest Serve"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack Attempts"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Attack Successes"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Block Successes"] [:th {:style "display: none", :class "split"} "Dig Successes"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States 1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-fla